I propose a YANI: magic staircases. (Inspired in part by the Hogwarts
staircases in Harry Potter.)

There should be a level-dependent chance (small but not vanishingly so)
for each of the staircases on a level that it is a magic staircase. A
magic staircase will do the following:

- every n turns, it will change its position in the level at random;
- every 2n turns, it has a chance of inverting (i.e. going to the level
above instead of down, or vice versa);
- every 20n turns (or some other high number), it goes into a state
where, if taken, it will lead the adventurer to an otherwise
inaccessible "obstacle course" dungeon branch filled with various
hazards (mazes, pits, lava, pools, traps of all varieties, as well as
-- of course, moving staircases.) In addition to these hazards, pieces
of the dungeon will move around unexpectedly as well ("The dungeon
rapidly reconfigures!") so you might suddenly find yourself standing on
the opposite side of the level. The entire branch is, of course,
non-teleport.
For those adventurers brave enough and patient enough to make it
through the branch, there should be some very nice prizes at the end.
(And a nice, stationary staircase to take you back to the ordinary
dungeon as well, of course.)

